---
description: Do not emit MSVC C4702 unreachable code.
globs: Source/**/*.h, Source/**/*.cpp
alwaysApply: true
---

# Unreachable code (C4702)
MSVC treats C4702 as an error. Every statement in a function must be reachable.

A `for` loop that always returns, breaks, or continues from the body makes the increment unreachable. When the function only needs the first match, use one iterator check.

```cpp
// C4702. ++It never runs.
for (TActorIterator<AJoA_GridManager> It(World); It; ++It)
{
	return *It;
}

// First match. No unreachable increment.
TActorIterator<AJoA_GridManager> It(World);
if (It)
{
	return *It;
}
```

The same rule covers any statement after an unconditional `return`, `break`, `continue`, or `throw`.